        "# Week 3 Assignment\n",
        "**Problem identification:** Predicting medical equipment failure (radiotherapy LINAC) at Kenyatta National Hospital"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aGYOTQDztVuw"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. My project problem and what I want the AI/ML system to do\n",
        "\n",
        "Kenyatta National Hospital (KNH) in Nairobi has had repeated breakdowns of its radiotherapy machine, the LINAC. When it stops working, the hospital falls back on an older cobalt machine and can only treat about half the usual number of cancer patients a day. Waiting times for radiotherapy have also gone up. I have seen this problem myself, and in most cases the machine is only fixed *after* it has already stopped.\n",
        "\n",
        "What I would like is an AI/ML system that looks at the machine's operating data and **predicts whether the machine is likely to fail soon**. If that works, the engineers could order spare parts and do servicing *before* the breakdown, so patients are not left waiting.\n",
        "\n",
        "In machine learning terms, this is a **classification** problem: for each reading, the answer is either \"likely to fail\" or \"not likely to fail\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "s1HdLErztVux"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. The data I would need\n",
        "\n",
        "For the real project, I would ideally need data from the LINAC itself:\n",
        "- error logs and fault codes\n",
        "- maintenance and repair history\n",
        "- how many hours the machine is used each day\n",
        "- machine age and how long parts have been in use\n",
        "- temperature and power readings\n",
        "- dates and times when it actually broke down\n",
        "\n",
        "I am not sure if KNH keeps this data in digital form, or if the manufacturer holds it. Hospital machine data is also private, so I could not find a public LINAC dataset. For now I will use a **stand-in dataset** that has the same kind of structure: machine sensor readings plus a column that says whether the machine failed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qA9KdcgTtVuz"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Dataset I chose\n",
        "\n",
        "I picked the **AI4I 2020 Predictive Maintenance Dataset** from the UCI Machine Learning Repository. It has 10,000 rows of machine readings (temperature, speed, torque, tool wear) and a label showing whether the machine failed. It is a synthetic dataset, made to look like real factory data, so it is not real LINAC data. But it lets me practise the same idea: using sensor readings to predict a failure.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/601/ai4i+2020+predictive+maintenance+dataset"
      ]
    },
